cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "eilj2: estimation-in-the-loop J2 formation-keeping"
type: software
version: v0.1.1
date-released: 2026-07-30
authors:
  - family-names: Pathak
    given-names: Ansh
    email: pathakansh10@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abc000cool/resonance-j2-eil"
url: "https://when-the-filter-lies.vercel.app"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21696854
abstract: >-
  Open-source reference implementation, Monte-Carlo campaign data, and manuscript
  for "Estimation-in-the-loop J2 formation-keeping: a Pareto characterization of
  relative-navigation accuracy versus delta-V cost": analytic relative-motion
  STMs (CW, Schweighart-Sedwick, Gim-Alfriend, Koenig-Guffanti-D'Amico),
  error-state EKF/UKF relative navigation, LQR/MPC/impulsive formation-keeping
  controllers, a J2-J4 numerical truth propagator cross-validated against Orekit,
  and a tiered Monte-Carlo campaign driver with deterministic seeding.
keywords:
  - spacecraft formation flying
  - relative navigation
  - Kalman filtering
  - filter consistency
  - J2 perturbation
  - formation keeping
  - reproducible research
